+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `features/todomvc.feature` and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Standing state
+- Greenfield shakedown repo, one commit: `todomvc: empty project with spec + template assets`.
+- No `RIGGING.md`, no `AGENTS.md`. Toolchain is fitted by `README.md`: Cucumber (`@cucumber/cucumber`) plus `happy-dom`, features under `features/`, step definitions under `features/support/`.
+- User directed the build: TodoMVC per `assets/app-spec.md`, base markup `assets/app-template.index.html`, vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence. The user released confirmation and ordered: author specs and the watchbill, then stop. No commit, push, or dispatch.
+
+## Decisions captured (so the next role needs no hidden chat)
+- Routing: implement with the native `hashchange` event, no Director dependency. This overrides the asset's Director suggestion to honour the user's vanilla-JS directive. Routes `#/`, `#/active`, `#/completed`; the app reads `location.hash` on load so the active filter survives reload.
+- localStorage store name: `todos-vanilla` (the `[framework]` token is `vanilla`).
+- Persisted item shape: keys `id`, `title`, `completed`; `editing` is runtime-only and never persisted. Pinned by the `@contract` scenario and `features/scantlings/todo-item.yaml`.
+- Keep `node_modules/todomvc-common` and `node_modules/todomvc-app-css` referenced by the template markup; keep the template's `base.css`/`index.css` links and the `css/app.css` override file. Follow the template DOM ids and classes exactly (`#main`, `#footer`, `.new-todo`, `#toggle-all`, `.todo-list`, `.toggle`, `.edit`, `.destroy`, `.todo-count`, `.filters`, `.clear-completed`).
+
+## Open
+- `package.json` does not yet list `todomvc-common` / `todomvc-app-css` as dependencies (the asset requires them). Crew or Shipwright reconciles this during the build; the files already sit in `node_modules` and the template links them.
+- No `RIGGING.md`; Shipwright fits it out at harbour. The watchbill is written but held: do not dispatch QM until the user releases this hold.
diff --git a/features/scantlings/todo-item.yaml b/features/scantlings/todo-item.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2fb1e0c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/scantlings/todo-item.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Scantling: todo-item
+# Mechanical shape every persisted todo record must satisfy.
+# Attested by the @contract scenario in features/todomvc.feature.
+store:
+  name: todos-vanilla
+  format: json-array
+item:
+  required-keys: [id, title, completed]
+  key-types:
+    id: string
+    title: string
+    completed: boolean
+  constraints:
+    - title is the trimmed, non-empty source text of the todo
+    - completed is false for a newly created todo
+  forbidden-keys: [editing]
diff --git a/features/todomvc.feature b/features/todomvc.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..03305ae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todomvc.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,194 @@
+# Source product spec: assets/app-spec.md
+# Base markup: assets/app-template.index.html
+# Build directive: vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence.
+Feature: TodoMVC application
+  As a person keeping a task list
+  I want to capture, complete, edit, filter, and persist todo items
+  So that the list survives reloads and stays easy to scan
+
+  Rule: Empty state hides the list chrome
+
+  Scenario: No todos hides the main and footer regions
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the element "#main" is hidden
+    And the element "#footer" is hidden
+
+  Rule: Creating todos
+
+  Scenario: New todo is created and the input is cleared on Enter
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "  Buy milk  " into ".new-todo"
+    And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+    Then the todo list contains one item with the label "Buy milk"
+    And the ".new-todo" input is empty
+
+  Scenario: New todo ignores blank input
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "    " into ".new-todo"
+    And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+    Then the todo list contains no items
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on load
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the ".new-todo" input is the active element
+
+  Rule: Completing and toggling todos
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all completes every todo
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 2 active todos
+    When the user checks "#toggle-all"
+    Then every todo item has the "completed" class
+    And every todo toggle checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all clears after completed items are cleared
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 2 completed todos
+    And the user clicks ".clear-completed"
+    Then "#toggle-all" is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all reflects all items completed
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 2 active todos
+    When the user checks each ".toggle"
+    Then "#toggle-all" is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all reflects an incomplete item
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 2 active todos
+    When the user checks the first ".toggle"
+    Then "#toggle-all" is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo marks it completed
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo
+    When the user checks ".toggle"
+    Then the todo item has the "completed" class
+    And the todo toggle checkbox is checked
+
+  Rule: Editing todos
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters edit mode
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo titled "Read a book"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo label
+    Then the todo item has the "editing" class
+    And the ".edit" input is focused
+    And the ".edit" input value is "Read a book"
+
+  Scenario: Edit saves on Enter
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo titled "Read a book"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo label
+    When the user changes the ".edit" input to "Read two books"
+    And the user presses Enter in ".edit"
+    Then the todo item does not have the "editing" class
+    And the todo label shows "Read two books"
+
+  Scenario: Edit saves on blur
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo titled "Read a book"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo label
+    When the user changes the ".edit" input to "Read two books"
+    And the user blurs ".edit"
+    Then the todo item does not have the "editing" class
+    And the todo label shows "Read two books"
+
+  Scenario: Edit removes the todo when blank
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo titled "Read a book"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo label
+    When the user changes the ".edit" input to "   "
+    And the user presses Enter in ".edit"
+    Then the todo list contains no items
+
+  Scenario: Edit discards changes on Escape
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo titled "Read a book"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo label
+    When the user changes the ".edit" input to "Read two books"
+    And the user presses Escape in ".edit"
+    Then the todo item does not have the "editing" class
+    And the todo label shows "Read a book"
+
+  Scenario: Destroy button removes a todo
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo
+    When the user clicks the todo ".destroy" button
+    Then the todo list contains no items
+
+  Rule: Counter and clearing completed todos
+
+  Scenario Outline: Counter pluralizes the active item count
+    Given the todo app is loaded with <active> active todo and <completed> completed todo
+    Then ".todo-count" shows the number "<count>" wrapped in a strong element
+    And ".todo-count" shows the word "<word>"
+
+    Examples:
+      | active | completed | count | word  |
+      | 0      | 0         | 0     | items |
+      | 1      | 0         | 1     | item  |
+      | 2      | 0         | 2     | items |
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes finished todos
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo and 1 completed todo
+    When the user clicks ".clear-completed"
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the remaining item is active
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden with no completed todos
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo and 0 completed todos
+    Then the ".clear-completed" button is hidden
+
+  Rule: Persistence
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist to localStorage on change
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "Write report" into ".new-todo"
+    And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+    Then the localStorage key "todos-vanilla" holds a JSON array
+    And the first record has the keys "id", "title", and "completed"
+    And the first record title is "Write report"
+    And the first record completed is false
+
+  Scenario: Todos reload from localStorage
+    Given the localStorage key "todos-vanilla" holds one todo titled "Write report"
+    When the todo app loads
+    Then the todo list contains one item with the label "Write report"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted across reload
+    Given the localStorage key "todos-vanilla" holds one todo titled "Write report"
+    When the todo app loads
+    Then no todo item has the "editing" class
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Persisted todo records conform to the item shape
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "Write report" into ".new-todo"
+    And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+    Then each record in the "todos-vanilla" store conforms to the "todo-item" schema in "features/scantlings/todo-item.yaml"
+
+  Rule: Routing
+    The app filters the list through native hash routing. The user directed a vanilla
+    JavaScript build with no preprocessors, so routing uses the window hashchange event
+    directly and adds no Director dependency. The active filter survives reload because the
+    app reads location.hash on load.
+
+  Scenario: Active filter defaults to all on first load
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo and 1 completed todo
+    Then the "All" filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the todo list contains 2 items
+
+  Scenario Outline: Route change filters the visible list
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo and 1 completed todo
+    When the route changes to "<route>"
+    Then the visible list shows <visible> item
+    And the "<label>" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+    Examples:
+      | route       | visible | label   |
+      | #/          | 2       | All     |
+      | #/active    | 1       | Active  |
+      | #/completed | 1       | Completed |
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo and 1 completed todo
+    And the route is "#/active"
+    When the todo app reloads
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the visible list shows 1 item
+
+  Scenario: Completing an item in a filtered view hides it
+    Given the todo app is loaded with 1 active todo and 1 completed todo
+    And the route is "#/active"
+    When the user checks ".toggle"
+    Then the visible list shows 0 items
